  "body": "A lone stream's prompt pass runs the GDN block as three launches: `fn_gdn_front` writes every row's q, k, v, g and beta as fp32 (41 KB a row, 63 MB for a 1,536-row chunk), `fn_gdn_chain_tpr` reads them back for the delta rule, and `fn_gdn_norm` reads the fp32 readouts again for the gated norm. On a GB10 the front is bound by DRAM (~240 GB/s), so overlapping it with the chain on a second stream hides almost nothing (measured: -0.5 % at 1,536 rows).\n\n`fn_gdn_fused` keeps those rows in shared memory:\n- 256 threads walk the chain with `fn_gdn_chain_tpr`'s code;\n- 128 producer threads make the next 16 rows' inputs with `fn_gdn_front`'s op sequence;\n- the same producers run the gated norm of the previous 16 rows with `fn_gdn_norm`'s.\n\nEvery row's arithmetic is unchanged, so the bits are too. The recurrence is row by row, so where the rows are cut (chunk size, resume point) does not change them either. Passes of 64 rows or more on one stream use it; `TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_FUSED=0` keeps the three launches.\n\n| GDN block, GB10 | three launches | fused |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1,024 rows | 1.277 ms | 1.040 ms |\n| 1,536 rows | 1.907 ms | 1.547 ms |\n| 4,096 rows | 5.008 ms | 4.078 ms |\n\nBytes (state, readouts, gated rows, sums) are equal from 64 to 4,096 rows.\n\n**Checks**\n- Kernel contract: nonfinite, repeat and 6 shapes bit-equal to front -> rows_to -> norm. The gate-5 record covers sm_80/86/89/120/121 (nvcc 13.0.88; no 13.2/13.3 override).\n- Full `zig build test -Dnvcc=/usr/local/cuda/bin/nvcc`: exit 0 (278/278 steps; 3,491 of 3,506 tests passed, 15 skipped). lean_check: 0 new against the merge base. `zig fmt` is clean.\n\n**Served Flash Next FP4-Local (MTP and prompt cache on, chunk 1,536)**\n\nToken hashes: 136 of 136 equal to main's. This covers greedy and seeded, c=1 and c=4, and cold, warm and resumed requests.\n\n| cold TTFT | main | fused |\n|---|---|---|\n| ~10k tokens | 7.81 / 7.85 s | 7.72 / 7.67 s |\n| ~38k tokens | 30.98 / 30.24 s | 30.02 / 29.93 s |\n\nThat is about -1.5 to -2 %.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- Branch `fn-gdn-fused` @ `c184e94c` (two commits), based on `main` @ `da275a360`; it test-merges cleanly onto today's `main` (`1705bf542`).\n- It touches `cuda_batch.zig` and `cuda_batch_state.zig`, which #1113, #1069 and #896 also change, and `contract_tests.zig`, as #958, #982, #987 and #1141 do. These are textual conflicts only (the fused path is one branch in the GDN block's launch).\n- The gate-5 record was made with nvcc 13.0.88 only; there's no 13.2/13.3 compiler on this machine.\n- Batched (multi-stream) prompt passes and passes under 64 rows keep the three launches. The 27B (`qwen3_5` CUDA) is unchanged: there, every fused form I tried was exact but slower (its prepare step is compute-heavy and four producer warps can't keep up).\n",
